WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.190
Puzzle one.

2
00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:04.040
A football crowd pours out of a stadium.

3
00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:05.910
How do people behave?

4
00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.170
Puzzle two.

5
00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:12.480
One person's whole childhood, from
first toys to first day at school.

6
00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:13.730
Puzzle three.

7
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.320
A polite smile.

8
00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:17.490
But what is going on behind it?

9
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:19.280
None of these fits in a lab.

10
00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:22.230
So how could a psychologist study them?

11
00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:25.570
In this mission, you'll open
a psychologist's toolkit:

12
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:29.750
questionnaires, interviews,
observations and case studies.

13
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.300
You'll find out which
questions give you numbers,

14
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:34.790
and which give you people's own words.

15
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:38.840
And you'll see why people don't
always give honest answers.

16
00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:43.080
Your mission: work out how a
psychologist could study all three.
